senses.gloss:
अश्रद्ध अ-श्रद्ध, अस्, आ, अम् (rt. धा with
श्रद्), not trusting in (with loc. c.); unbelieving;
(आ), f. want of trust, unbelief.

अश्रम अ-श्रम, अस्, m. (rt. श्रम्), freedom
from fatigue, freshness; absence of toil, laziness;
(अस्, आ, अम्), Ved. indefatigable.

आ-श्रित, अस्, आ, अम्, inhabiting, dwelling in, resort-
ing to as a retreat or asylum; having recourse to;
following, practising, observing; using, employing;
receiving anything as an inherent or integral part;
taking one's station at a window or seat &c.; depend-
ant on, a dependant; (आनि), n. pl. the objects perceived
by the senses and मनस् or mind.
—आश्रित-त्व, अम्,
n. dependance.

अश्रेयस् अ-श्रेयस्, आन्, असी, अस्, not the better,
inferior, worse; worthless, useless, unprofitable, bad;
(अस्), n. mischief, unhappiness.
